$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of α-(2,4-Dinitrophenylthio)acetic Acid, 1. Mercaptoacetic acid
(26 mmol) in 20 mL of CHCl3 was slowly added to a solution of 5 g (26
mmol) of 2,4-dinitrofluorobenzene mixed with 7 mL of triethylamine at
room temperature. Extractions were carried out with HCl (1 M) and then
twice with water. The product was separated, dried over magnesium sulfate
(MgSO4), and filtered. Yellow crystals were then recrystallized from
CHCl3. A yield of 6.1 g (88%). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 9.06 (s, 1H, -Ar, J m =
3.0 Hz); δ 8.27 (dd, 1H, -Ar, J m = 3.0 Hz, J o = 9.0 Hz); δ 7.75 (d, 1H,
-Ar, J o = 9.0 Hz); δ 3.76 (s, 2H, -SCH 2COOH). Elemental analysis:
(found) % C, 36.80; % H, 2.53; % N, 10.71; % S, 12.30; (calculated) % C,
37.21; % H, 2.34; % N, 10.85; % S, 12.42.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
