$DATUM Synthesis of 4-[4-(Butylthio)tetrafluorophenylazo]-aniline (2e). To an
ethanol solution (40 mL) of 4-(pentafluorophenylazo) aniline 2 (1.0 g,
3.5 mmol) was added a butanethiol solution (6 mL) of sodium
butanethiolate (4 mmol) and the mixture stirred at room temperature for
20 h. After the reaction was completed, the mixture was poured into
aqueous dilute sodium hydroxide solution. The product was extracted with
dichloromethane, washed with a dilute sodium hydroxide solution, water,
and dried. After concentrating the extract, the product was isolated by
column chromatography (SiO2, CHCl3-C6H14). Yield 88%. mp 131-133°C; 1H
NMR (CDCl3) δ = 0.92 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H), 1.44 (sext, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H),
1.58 (quint, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 2.97 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 4.26 (br s, 2H),
6.73 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H), 7.83 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H); 19F NMR (CDCl3, ext
CF3COOH) δ = -57.4 (2F), -74.1 (2F); EIMS (70 eV) m/z (rel intensity) 357
(M+; 27), 120 (38), 92 (100).
