$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Aryl Arenedithiocarboxylates 3; General Procedure: To the stirred red
solution of the sodium arenedithiocarboxylate 1 (10 mmol) in t-BuOH
(15mL) is slowly added the appropriate iodonium salt 2 (10 mmol). The
resultant mixture is stirred at 70°C for the time given in the Table. The
solvent is removed under reduced pressure, H2O (15 mL) is added to the
residue, and the resultant mixture is extracted with CH2Cl2 (3x 10 mL).
The extract is washed with H2O (10 mL) and dried (MgSO4). The solvent is
removed, hexane (10 mL) is added to the residue, and the product is
allowed to crystallize in a refrigerator overnight. The crude product is
isolated and recrystallized from benzene/hexane. Product 3k, yield 88%.
mp: 77-78 °C; Molecular Formulab: C14H11NO2S2 (289.3); 1H-NMR(CDCl3/TMS)
δ : 2.43 (s, 3H); 7.20-7.40 (m, 4H). 7.60-7.84 (m, 2H); 8.26-8.44 (m,
2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Polyvalent iodine in synthesis. 3. An efficient method for the synthesis
of aryl arenedithiocarboxylates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chen, Zhen Chu; Jin, You Yuan; Yang, Rui Yang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (1988), (9), 723-4

