$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-methoxphenyl-3'-tolylsulfide 3-Bromotoluene (1.97 mL, 16.26 mmol, 1.0
equiv), 2-propanol (17 mL), potassium hydroxide (2.11 g, 32.52 mmol, 2.0
equiv), tetrakis (triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (188 mg, 0.163mmol,
0.01 equiv), (S)-BINAP (203 mg., 0.325 mmol, 0.02 equiv) and 4-
methoxybenzenethiol (2.0 mL, 16.26 mmol, 1.0 equiv) were heated under a
nitrogen atmosphere for 6-8 h at 83 °C. After the reaction was completed
it was cooled (<30 °C) and quenched with water (17 mL) which resulted in
formation of an oil. The mixture so formed was allowed to granulate for 1
h at 10-15 °C. The resultant slurry was filtered and the filtrate
concentrated to form an oil, added water (30 mL) and acidified. The
solution was extracted with dichloromethane, sodium bicarbonate, and
filtered though cotton. Condensed and placed the brown oil on the high
vacuum overnight. Obtained a brown oil7, 3.28 g.
4-methoxphenyl-3'-tolylsulfide, Yield 87.5 % m/z 230; C14H14OS requires:
C, 73.0; H, 6.13; S, 13.9. Found: C, 73.2; H, 6.30; S, 14.2%; 1H NMR (300
MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 7.42 (d, 2H), 7.20 (t, 2H), 7.01 (t, 2H), 6.91 (d, 2H),
3.79 (s, 3H), 2.24 (s, 3H); IR (cm-1) νmax; 1593, 1493, 1288, 1247.
