$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Nickel-Mediated Intermolecular C−S
Cross-coupling of Various Thiols and Aryl Iodides General Procedure A To
a stirred slurry of Zn (130 mg, 2 mmol) and NiCl2 (38 mg, 0.3 mmol) in
pyridine (0.5 mL) was added ethyl crotonate (0.12 mL, 0.9 mmol) or
bipyridine (57 mg, 0.36 mmol) at room temperature. Then the temperature
rose to 55 °C and vigorous stirring was continued for 15 minutes. The
resulting Ni(0) complex was cooled to room temperature, to which the
solution of aryl iodide (1 mmol) in pyridine (0.5 mL) was added quickly.
After 2 min, the solution of thiol (1~1.2 mmol) in MeOH (2 mL) was added
dropwise over a 15-min period. After 3.5 h, the mixture was filtered with
a short plug of silica (elution with 60 mL Et2O) and washed with HCl
(1N), water and brine, dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated. The
crude product was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel to
afford desired thioether. 4-Methoxyphenyl phenyl sulfide (1a)1 1a was
prepared (70% yield) according to General Procedure A. 4-Acetylphenyl
phenyl sulfide (1r)6 1r was prepared according to General Procedure A.
White solid (87% yield). Rf = 0.43 (petroleum ether/EtOAc = 5 : 1); Mp.
66.1-67.2 °C; IR (film): νmax = 3078, 3059, 1679, 1587, 1436, 1398, 1358,
1267, 1089, 1064, 957, 846, 820, 759, 694 cm−1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3):
δ = 7.81 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.51−7.48 (m, 2H), 7.40−7.39 (m, 3H), 7.21
(d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 2.55 (s, 3H) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
197.0, 144.9, 134.5, 133.8 (2C), 132.1, 129.6 (2C), 128.9 (2C), 128.8
(2C), 127.4, 26.4 ppm; EI−MS (70 eV): m/z: 228 [M]+, 213, 184, 152, 139.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM dropwise addition of thiol solution stage 3, in-situ generated catalyst
(stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Mediated Inter- and Intramolecular C-S Coupling of Thiols and
Thioacetates with Aryl Iodides at Room Temperature
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Xu, Xiao-Bo; Liu, Jian; Zhang, Jian-Jian; Wang, Ya-Wen; Peng, Yu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(3), 550-553

