$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of Aryl
Sulfides: To a stirred solution of iodobenzene (1.1 mmol) and In(OTf)3
(10 mol%) in dry DMSO (2.0 mL) was added thiophenol (1.0 mmol) followed
by TMEDA (20 mol%) and KOH (2.0 eq) under nitrogen atmosphere. The
reaction mixture was then stirred at 135 °C for 24 h. The progress of the
reaction was monitored by TLC and then allowed to cool to room
temperature. Diethyl ether (5 mL) was added and the organic phase was
separated, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and purified by chromatography on
silica gel to afford the corresponding coupling product.
4-(phenylthio)phenol (entry 14, Table 3):1 colorless oil 1H NMR (200 MHz,
CDCl3, TMS): δ = 7.39 (d, 2H, J = 8.05), 7.31 - 7.24 (m, 2H),7.20 - 7.12
(m, 3H), 6.83 (d, 2H, J = 8.05), 4.90 (bs, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3,
TMS): δ = 155.8, 138.1, 135.0, 128.5, 127.8, 125.7, 124.5, 116.4
