$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Intra and
Intermolecular C-S bond formation: An oven-dried flask was charged with
CuI (5 mol %), L5 (10 mol %), dithiocarbamate (1 mmol), iodobenzene (1.1
equiv), K2CO3 (3 equiv), and solvent DMSO (1 mL). The flask was kept in a
pre-heated oil bath at 90 oC. Heating was continued for 4 hrs after which
the reaction mixture was cooled and admixed with water (5 mL). The
product was extracted with ethylacetate (2 x 10 mL), organic layer dried
over anh.Na2SO4, concentrated under reduced pressure, and purified over
column of silica gel (EtOAc: Hexane as eluents) to give product 1a in 86
% isolated yield. The identity and purity of the products were confirmed
by spectroscopic analysis. 2-(Phenylthio)benzo[d]thiazole or
2-Phenylsulfanyl-benzothiazole (1a).
2-(4-Nitrophenylthio)benzo[d]thiazole or
2-p-Nitrophenylsulfanyl-benzothiazole (1d). Yellow solid; Mp. 105 – 107
°C (Lit9d M.p.95-96 °C); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.38 (t, 1H, J = 7.6
Hz), 7.48 (t, 1H, J = 7.6 Hz), 7.77 (d, 2H, J = 7.6 Hz), 7.96 (d, 1H, J =
8.2 Hz), 8.23 (d, 2H, J = 7.6 Hz); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 121.3,
122.9, 124.6, 125.6, 126.8, 132.8, 136.3, 140.1, 147.9, 153.5, 163.0; IR
(KBr): 3094, 2840, 1597, 1518, 1455, 1340, 1002, 843, 765 cm-1. Anal.
Calcd for C13H8N2O2S2 (288.34): C 54.15, H 2.80, N 9.72, S 22.24; found C
54.08, H 2.79, N 9.68, S 22.16. Crystallographic description of 1d:
Crystal dimension (mm): 0.29 x 0.21 x 0.16. C13H8N2O2S2, Mr = 288.33.
Monoclinic, space group P2(1)/n; a = 7.4427(6) Å, b = 9.3482(7) Å, c =
18.2369(14) Å; α = 90.00°, β = 95.639(4)°, γ = 90.00°, V = 1262.71(17)
Å3; Z = 4; ρcal = 1.517 mg/m3; μ(mm-1) = 0.419; F (000) = 592; Reflection
collected / unique = 4090 / 3019; Refinement method = Full-matrix
least-squares on F 2; Final R indices [I>2σl ] R1 = 0.0909, wR2 = 0.2170,
R indices (all data) R1 = 0.0711, wR2 = 0.1839; goodness of fit = 1.192.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Intra- and Intermolecular C-S Bond Formation Using a Single Catalytic
