$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ethyl(4'-methoxy-3-methylbiphenyl-2-yl)sulfane (9). A flame-dried
microwave 10 ml glass vial equipped was charged with NaH (60% w/w in
mineral oil, 16 mg, 0.4 mmol, 2.0 equiv.), evacuated and backfilled with
argon. THF (0.5 ml) was added, followed by a dropwise addition of EtSH
(36 μl, 0.5 mmol, 2.5 equiv.). After 45 minutes, a solution of complex
3aa-Cr(CO)3 (70.5 mg, 0.2 mmol. 1.0 equiv.) in THF (0.5 ml) was added
dropwise and the resulting yellow suspension was stirred for 24 h at 30
°C. Then, methanol (100 μl) was added and the solution was then loaded on
a short silica plug (2 x 4 cm) and eluted with THF (3 x 5 ml). The
solution was placed on a crystallizing dish and exposed to the light
(table lamp 60W) for 6 h and then concentrated in vacuo. Purification via
flash chromatography (gradient 0.01-5% Et2O in hexane). The title product
as bright yellow oil in 87% yield. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) =
7.37 (d, J = 10.2 Hz, 2H), 7.23 (d, J = 4.3 Hz, 2H), 7.13 (app. t, J =
4.4 Hz, 1H), 6.94 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 3.86 (s, 3H), 2.59 (s, 3H), 2.33
(q, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 0.95 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3):
δ (ppm) = 158.7, 147.0, 143.2, 135.1, 132.7, 130.8, 129.3, 128.7, 127.8,
113.2, 55.4, 29.3, 22.5, 14.7. IR: ν = 2958, 1608, 1508, 1454, 1244,
1051, 784 cm-1. HRMS EI+ m/z calcd. C16H19OS: [M+H]+ 259.1151; found:
[M+H]+ 259.1148.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical (in stage 3), 60W used in stage 3
