$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: In the catalytic reactions, to a yellow
suspension of 8 (2.0 mg, 3 μmol), 4-fluoroiodobenzene (40 μL, 0.35 mmol)
and the appropriate thiol (37 μL, 0.30 mmol) in benzene, was added NaOtBu
(33.5 mg, 0.35 mmol) and the mixture was stirred for 2 h at RT. The
progress was monitored by GC. The orange suspension was filtered and the
solution was evaporated. The residue was purified on a silica gel column
to afford the product (from 2-thiocresol).
(2,6-dimethylphenyl)(4-fluorophenyl) sulfide from 2,6-dimethylthiophenol:
60.5 mg, 87% yield. 1H NMR 7.32-7.24 (m, Ar-H, 3H), 7.01-6.93 (m, Ar-H,
4H), 2.52 (s, CH3, 6H); 13C{1H} 160.80 (d, JFC = 243.2 Hz, C-F), 143.76
(s), 133.13 (d, J= 3.2 Hz), 129.42 (s), 128.64 (s), 127.60 (d, JFC = 7.7
Hz), 116.17 (s), 115.95 (s), 21.91 (s); 19F{1H} -117.28 (s); EI-MS M+
(Calc. for C14H13FS) 232 (232).
