$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Bromo-3-fluorobenzene (2.1 mL, 18.77 mmol, 1.0 equiv), 2-propanol (20
mL), potassium hydroxide (2.44 g, 37.54 mmol, 2.0 equiv),
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (108 mg, 0.094 mmol, 0.005
equiv), (S)-BINAP (117 mg., 0.188 mmol, 0.01 equiv) and
4-fluorobenzenethiol (2.0 mL, 18.77 mmol, 1.0 equiv) were heated under a
nitrogen atmosphere for 4 h at 83 °C. After the reaction was completed it
was cooled (<30 °C) and quenched with water (20 mL) which resulted in a
small exotherm (+2 °C) and a formation of an oil. The mixture was allowed
to stir for 1 hr at 10-15 °C, neutralized using concentrated HCl and
extracted with ethyl acetate, washed with brine and dried over magnesium
sulfate, filtered and concentrated to dryness. Obtained a brown oil, 3.64
g, 87%:m/z 222; Purified by column chromatography (silica gel/ethyl
acetate/hexane) to obtain pure sample, yellow oil11 yield 3.18 g.
3-fluorophenyl-4'-fluorophenylsulfide, Yield 87% m/z 222; Purified by
column chromatography (silica gel/ethyl acetate/hexane) to obtain pure
sample, yellow oil11 yield 3.18 g, 76% C12 H8F2S requires: C, 64.85; H,
3.63; S, 14.4. Found: C, 65.1; H, 3.71; S, 14.6%; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 7.44 (m, 2H), 7.22 (m, 1H), 7.07 (m, 2H) 6.97 (m, 1H), 6.85 (m, 2H).
