$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A General procedure for the one-pot C-S
cross-coupling reaction. To a glass vial charged with PEG-600 (3 mL) was
added nitroaryl halide (0.5 mmol), thiol (0.75 mmol), and KOH (84 mg, 3
equiv). The resulting mixture was stirred at 100 °C and monitored by TLC.
Upon completion of the reaction (approx. 2 h), the mixture was cooled to
room temperature, poured into water (10 mL), and extracted several times
with ethyl acetate (15×3 mL). The combined organic layers were washed
with water, dried over Na2SO4, and filtered. The solvent was removed in
vacuo and the residue was purified by column chromatography (silica gel,
eluent: hexane/ethyl acetate) to afford the aryl sulfide product.
4-[(4-methylphenyl)thio]benzenamine (3g). Obtained as a yellow solid in
87% yield. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.30-7.28 (td, 2H), 7.11-7.09 (d,
2H), 7.07-7.04 (d, 2H), 6.67-6.64 (td, 2H), 3.77(br s, 2 H), 2.30 (s, 3H)
ppm; 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 146.7, 135.6, 135.5, 135.4, 129.7, 128.3,
121.7, 115.9, 21.0 ppm; HR EIMS 215.0777 m/z (calcd. for C13H13NS:
215.0769).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Pot Synthesis of Amine-Substituted Aryl Sulfides and
Benzo[b]thiophene Derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Duan, Zhongyu; Ranjit, Sadananda; Liu, Xiaogang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2010), 12(10), 2430-2433

