$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 4,5-bis(tert-butylsulfanyl)phthalonitrile (1)
tert-Butanethiol (13.3 g, 147 mmol), 4,5-dichlorophthalonitrile (3) (9.7
g, 49 mmol), and anhydrous potassium carbonate (80 g, 590 mmol) were
stirred in N,N′-dimethylformamide (DMF) (100 mL) under a nitrogen
atmosphere overnight at room temperature. Water was then added to the
reaction mixture and the stirring continued 2 h more. The resulting
precipitate was then filtered, thoroughly washed with water, and
crystallized from ethanol. Yield: 12.8 g (86%). White powder. C16H20N2S2,
MW 304.47. mp: 163-165°C. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ, ppm 7.86 (2H, s, Ar-CH),
1.46 (18H, s, CH3). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ, ppm 146.96 (Ar-CH), 136.99
(Ar-C-S), 115.19 (Ar-C-CN), 112.56 (CN), 49.46 (C-S), 31.04 (CH3).
ATR-IR: ν max, cm-1 3068, 2978, 2964, 2939, 2899, 2867, 2228 (CN), 1505,
1451, 1396, 1366, 1283, 1221, 1158 (Ar-S-C), 1105, 931, 873 (C-H). LC-MS
(ESI) m/z: calcd for C16H20N2NaS2: 327.099; found 327.107.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 4,5-, 3,6-, and 3,4,5,6-tert-Butylsulfanylphthalonitriles: synthesis and
comparative structural and spectroscopic analyses
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kumru, Ufuk; Dumoulin, Fabienne; Jeanneau, Erwann; Yuksel, Fatma;
Cabezas, Yari; Zorlu, Yunus; Ahsen, Vefa
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Structural Chemistry (2012), 23(1), 175-183

