$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2,5-Bis(methylthio)terephthalaldehyde (1).To a solution of
2,5-dibromoterephthalaldehydeS1 (500 mg, 1.7 mmol) in DMF (30 mL) was
added sodium methanethiolate (280 mg, 4 mmol), and the mixture was
stirred for 10 min at rt. The mixture was poured into diluted
hydrochloride solution (ca. 1M, 60 mL), and extracted with chloroform
(100 mL × 3). The combined organic layer was washed with water (50 mL),
dried (MgSO4), and concentrated in vacuo. The residual solid was purified
by column chromatography on silica gel eluted with dichloromethane (Rf =
0.4) to give 1. Pale orange solid.Yield(335 mg, 87%). Mp 188-189 °C. 1H
NMR (400 Hz, CDCl3) δ 10.42 (s, 2H, CHO), 7.80 (s, 2H, ArH), 2.58 (s, 6H,
SCH3); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 16.5, 130.1, 136.3, 139.8, 190.7; EIMS
(70 eV) m/z = 226 (M+). Anal. Calcd for C10H10O2S2: C, 53.07; H, 4.45.
Found: C, 53.26; H, 4.48%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
