$DATUM 2-(Isopropylthio)-5-nitrobenzaldehyde (21). To
2-fluoro-5-nitrobenzaldehyde (5.8 g, 34.2 mmol) and 2-thiopropane (3.5
mL, 37.7 mmol) in DMF (20 mL) was added potassium carbonate (5.2 g, 37.7
mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at 70 °C overnight. The crude
reaction mixture was filtered and washed with ethyl acetate. The combined
filtrate and washings were concentrated. The residue was re-dissolved in
ethyl acetate and washed with water (3x) and then dried over sodium
sulfate. Purification was performed by flash column chromatography. 21
(6.7 g, 87% yield) as an oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ ppm 1.36 (d, J
=6.60 Hz, 6 H) 3.73 - 3.93 (m, 1 H) 7.77 (d, J =9.05 Hz, 1 H) 8.36 (dd, J
=9.05, 2.69 Hz, 1 H) 8.71 (d, J =2.69 Hz, 1 H) 10.20 (s, 1 H). MS (ESI)
m/z 226.1 [M + H]+.
