$DATUM Typical experimental procedure of Pd-catalyzed C-S cross-coupling
reactions and the sequential indium-mediated allylation and allenylation
reactions (Table 4) Reaction with 2-iodobenzaldehyde (4a) (Table 4, entry
1, 5a) : To a suspension of Pd(OAc)2 (2.3 mg, 0.010mmol, 2.0 mol%) and
Xantphos (6.2 mg, 0.011mmol, 2.1 mol%) in DMF (0.8 mL) was added
2-iodobenzaldehyde (4a) (116.0 mg, 0.50 mmol) in DMF (0.5 mL) at room
temperature under a nitrogen atmosphere. After being stirred for 5 min,
(4-MeO-C6H4S)3In (89.0 mg, 0.167 mmol) and DIPEA (87.0 μL, 0.50 mmol) in
DMF (0.7 mL) was transferred via double-ended needle and the mixture was
stirred at 90 °C for 2 h. Reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature
and transferred to mixture of indium (58.0 mg, 0.50 mmol), NaI (120.0 mg,
0.80 mmol) and prenyl bromide (93.0 μL, 0.81 mmol) in DMF (0.8 mL). After
being stirring for 2 h at room temperature, the reaction mixture was
quenched with NaHCO3 (sat. aq.). The aqueous layer was extracted with
ether (3 × 20 mL), and the combined organics were washed with water and
brine, dried with anhydrous MgSO4, filtered and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (EtOAc:Hexane=1:10) to give desired product 5a as pale
yellow oil (135.0 mg, 86%). 1H-NMR(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.48 (d, J = 7.8 Hz,
1H), 7.30 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.18 (dd, J = 7.4, 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.10 (dd,
J = 7.4, 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.04 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.86 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H),
6.05 (dd, J = 10.7, 17.5 Hz, 1H), 5.22 (d, J = 3.4 Hz, 1H), 5.16 (d, J =
10.7 Hz, 1H), 5.09 (d, J = 17.5 Hz, 1H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 2.11 (d, J = 3.4
Hz, 1H), 1.12 (s, 3H), 1.05 (s, 3H); 13C-NMR(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 159.4,
145.0, 140.5, 137.1, 134.3, 130.3, 128.4, 127.9, 125.9, 125.8, 115.0,
113.9, 75.6, 55.3, 43.3, 24.6, 21.4; IR (Neat) 3466, 3060, 2965, 2836,
2044, 1592, 1494, 1247, 1030. 827 cm-1; HRMS (EI) calcd for C19H22O2S M+
314.1340, found 314.1341.
