$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Phenyl(2-(phenylthio)phenyl)methanone (1g) To a solution of thiophenol
(1.9 mL, 18 mmol) in DMF (50 mL) at 0 °C was added sodium hydride (0.72
g, 60% disp. in mineral oil, 18 mmol) and the mixture was allowed to warm
to room temperature over 15 min. To this mixture was added a solution of
2-chlorobenzophenone (3.27 g, 15 mmol) in DMF (10 mL) and the resulting
solution was heated to 140 °C for 3 h. The solution was allowed to cool
to room temperature and poured into water (100 mL). The solution was
extracted with EtOAc (2 × 50 mL) and the combined organic extracts were
washed with brine (50 mL) dried (Mg2SO4) and concentrated in vacuo. The
crude product was purified by column chromatography (20% ether/petrol)
and recrystallized (ether/petrol). The product (4.5 g, 86%) as a
colourless powder. M.p. 50-51 °C (lit. m.p.2 51-52 °C); 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.81-7.84 (m, 2H), 7.57-7.61 (m, 1H), 7.44-7.48 (m, 3H),
7.24-7.39 (m, 8H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 196.4, 139.1, 137.3, 137.2,
134.6, 133.1, 132.7, 131.3, 130.9, 130.1, 129.6, 129.3, 128.4, 127.8,
125.8; ν max (film)/cm-1 1664, 1314, 925, 739, 689, 635.
